\"; grep -n \"gptel-fork\\|GPTEL_FORK\" /root/i.ar/iar.sh 2>/dev/null | head -10"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[11:09:56] /root/i.ar/emacs.d/init.d/core/iar-gptel-setup.el\n===\n=== env in container? ===\nEMACBOROS_GPTEL_FORK_PATH=/root/.emacs.d/gptel-fork\n=== emacboros.sh fork flag ===\n\n[t+02:48/60:00 c20/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_wmy7uoiz","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"fork\\|load-path\" /root/i.ar/emacs.d/init.d/core/iar-gptel-setup.el | head -15"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[11:09:57] 5:(defvar iar-fork-path)\n7:;; If a gptel fork path is configured, prepend it to load-path so the\n8:;; fork takes precedence over the ELPA-installed package.  This is used\n11:(when (and iar-fork-path\n12:           (stringp iar-fork-path)\n13:           (file-directory-p iar-fork-path))\n14:  (message \"[gptel] Using fork from %s (overriding ELPA package)\" iar-fork-path)\n15:  (add-to-list 'load-path iar-fork-path))\n\n[t+02:50/60:00 c21/300]"}]
